  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound 2-(3-Hydroxy-5-methoxyphenyl)-3-methoxyfuro[2,3-h]chromen-4-one and the serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1, through a series of target interactions. The compound is identified as a target of the splicing factor, proline- and glutamine-rich, which in turn is targeted by Gardenin. Additionally, the compound is also a target of another compound, 5,7,2'-Trihydroxy-3',4'-methylenedioxy-6,8-dimethyl homoisoflavone, which also targets CDC2L1. This indicates that the compound may act through a shared pathway involving splicing factors and their downstream targets. The evidence suggests that the compound may influence the activity of CDC2L1 through a mechanism involving splicing factors, potentially through the regulation of protein kinases or other downstream signaling components. The integration of these targets highlights a possible role for the compound in modulating cellular processes through the regulation of splicing and kinase activity.",
